%I A401443 #22 Nov 05 2026 20:25:45
%S A401443 59044,59049,1015,59049,0,59049,59045,59049,3116
%N A401443 From a test by Paul Cooijmans (item 27 of Short Test for Genius).
%C A401443 Short Test for Genius, question 27.
%H A401443 Paul Cooijmans, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20031006141136/http://members.chello.nl/p.cooijmans/gliaweb/tests/tfg/tfgshort.html">Short Test For Genius</a>
%e A401443 The even-position terms are all 59049=9^5. The odd-position terms are derived from the digits of 59049: reverse the digits, raise each to the power 5 then subtract the matching forward digit: 9^5-5=59044, 4^5-9=1015, 0^5-0=0, 9^5-4=59045, 5^5-9=3116.
%Y A401443 Cf. A027747, A122549.
